# Safe Harbor — environment template.
#
# Copy to /etc/safe-harbor/.env and fill in real values. Never commit the
# real file. The installer generates /etc/safe-harbor/.env from this
# template, replacing __RANDOM_HEX__ with openssl rand -hex 32.

# A2A peer credentials. Each peer's token lives in the environment of the
# side that CALLS it (never in config files or systemd units):
#   A2A_TOKEN_<PEERNAME> — bearer token used when calling peer <PEERNAME>
# (set e.g. A2A_TOKEN_SPECIALIST in the manager's shell / unit environment)

# Hermes A2A server-side security (manager + specialist, per Hermes docs):
# A2A_BEARER_TOKEN is the shared inbound token; A2A_PEER_TOKENS maps
# peer-name:token pairs ("manager:tok1,specialist:tok2"); A2A_TRUSTED_PEERS
# is the allow-list of authenticated identities.
# A2A_BEARER_TOKEN=
# A2A_PEER_TOKENS=
# A2A_TRUSTED_PEERS=

# Explicit A2A bind. Hermes refuses a non-loopback bind unless a token is
# configured — do not set this to 0.0.0.0. Default: 127.0.0.1
# A2A_HOST=127.0.0.1
# A2A_PUBLIC_URL=http://127.0.0.1:9900/

# jñāpakaṁ server (loopback only in Gen1). If MEMORY_AUTH_TOKEN is set it
# becomes mandatory for every request.
# MEMORY_AUTH_TOKEN=

# Restate (loopback-only via firewall in Gen1; no bind key exists upstream).
# RESTATE_NODE_NAME=safeharbor-manager